, the tool to use here is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command to get the ConfigMap. That way, I can inspect the configuration file and see if there are any errors in the MongoDB setup.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nTo inspect the MongoDB configuration causing the crash, I will retrieve the contents of the `url-shorten-mongodb` ConfigMap. This will reveal if there are misconfigurations (e.g., incorrect data directories, permissions, or MongoDB-specific settings) preventing the container from starting successfully.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get configmap url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network -o yaml"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=482, prompt_tokens=4098, total_tokens=4580, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbbe-5ce0-7a01-99ec-1e09f7f4adc8-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4098, 'output_tokens': 482, 'total_tokens': 4580}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='91390f0d-9f38-4b9b-8051-50d3a2fcff37')]]
