 the data is there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn\'t mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is using the tls.pem from the secret, but the pod\'s volumes aren\'t set up to mount the secret. So even though the secret exists, the container doesn\'t have access to it because it\'s not mounted. The user needs to check the pod\'s volume mounts to see if the secret is attached. \n\nBut the user already used kubectl describe pod and saw that the volume mounts include the ConfigMap but not the Secret. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn\'t. So the solution would be to update the pod\'s spec to include the secret as a volume mount. However, the user can\'t modify the pod directly; they need to update the Deployment or StatefulSet that\'s managing it. \n\nSince the user is supposed to submit the root cause, they should explain that the mongodb-tls secret exists but isn\'t mounted to /etc/tls/, causing MongoDB to fail. The user should be informed to mount the secret in the pod\'s configuration.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\ntool call: {"command": "kubectl describe configmap url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 362, 'prompt_tokens': 5088, 'total_tokens': 5450, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-1f7d-7662-99c9-d5afac15bea3-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5088, 'output_tokens': 362, 'total_tokens': 5450}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4632323e-031d-41a7-9f36-637b59254303'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is dealing with a MongoDB pod that's crashing with a CrashLoopBackOff status. From the previous steps, they checked the pod's logs and description, found that the container is crashing because it can't find the TLS certificate. They looked into the ConfigMap and found that the MongoDB configuration points to /etc/tls/tls.pem. Then they checked the Secrets in the namespace and found a mongodb-tls secret that has tls.pem, but when they described the secret, it shows that the data is there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn't mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is using the tls.pem from the secret, but the pod's volumes aren't set up to mount the secret. So even though the secret exists, the container doesn't have access to it because it's not mounted. The user needs to check the pod's volume mounts to see if the secret is attached. \n\nBut the user already used kubectl describe pod and saw that the volume mounts include the ConfigMap but not the Secret. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn't. So the solution would be to update the pod's spec to include the secret as a volume mount. However, the user can't modify the pod directly; they need to update the Deployment or StatefulSet that's managing it. \n\nSince the user is supposed to submit the root cause, they should explain that the mongodb-tls secret exists but isn't mounted to /etc/tls/, causing MongoDB to fail. The user should be informed to mount the secret in the pod's configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe configmap url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-96ad37c2585ebf98', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 376, 'prompt_tokens': 6145, 'total_tokens': 6521, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-3120-73b1-aaf3-2097dd7acedb-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe configmap url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-96ad37c2585ebf98', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6145, 'output_tokens': 376, 'total_tokens': 6521}), ToolMessage(content='Name:         url-shorten-mongodb\nNamespace:    social-network\nLabels:       app.kubernetes.io/managed-by=Helm\n              socialnetwork/service=url-shorten-mongodb\nAnnotations:  meta.helm.sh/release-name: social-network\n              meta.helm.sh/release-namespace: social-network\n\nData\n====\nmongod.conf:\n----\nnet:\n  tls:\n    mode: requireTLS\n    certificateKeyFile: /etc/tls/tls.pem\n\n\n\nBinaryData\n====\n\nEvents:  <none>\n', id='bcd45e1f-8cbd-44df-9dbf-bdb5f085208e', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-96ad37c2585ebf98'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='1087d603-9fa5-4d70-84d5-f331ac3411da')]]
