tc/tls/. \n\nSo the next tool call should be to exec_kubectl_cmd_safely to edit the Deployment. The user needs to apply the changes to mount the Secret. After making the change, they should wait a few seconds for the pod to restart and check if the issue is resolved. If the pod starts successfully, the problem is fixed. If not, they might need to check the logs again or adjust the mount path.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\ntool call: {"command": "kubectl edit deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 388, 'prompt_tokens': 5501, 'total_tokens': 5889, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-7e4d-7da3-bbb8-15aaf1a59678-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5501, 'output_tokens': 388, 'total_tokens': 5889}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='904c3a93-50e1-42fc-ae17-370b6a25b83a'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is dealing with a MongoDB pod that's crashing with a CrashLoopBackOff status. From the previous steps, they checked the pod's logs and description, found that the container is crashing because it can't find the TLS certificate. They looked into the ConfigMap and found that the MongoDB configuration points to /etc/tls/tls.pem. Then they checked the Secrets in the namespace and found a mongodb-tls secret that has tls.pem, but when they described the secret, it shows that the data is there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn't mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is using the tls.pem from the secret, but the pod's volumes aren't set up to mount the secret. So even though the secret exists, the container doesn't have access to it because it's not mounted. The user needs to check the pod's volume mounts to see if the secret is attached. \n\nBut the user already used kubectl describe pod and saw that the volume mounts include the ConfigMap but not the Secret. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn't. So the solution would be to update the pod's spec to include the secret as a volume mount. However, the user can't modify the pod directly; they need to update the Deployment or StatefulSet that's managing it. \n\nSince the user is supposed to submit the root cause, they should explain that the mongodb-tls secret exists but isn't mounted to /etc/tls/, causing MongoDB to fail. The user should be informed to mount the secret in the pod's configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl edit deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-85a5ff3950790418', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 375, 'prompt_tokens': 6557, 'total_tokens': 6932, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-90b4-7ad0-a87c-5ef12a0e7996-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl edit deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-85a5ff3950790418', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6557, 'output_tokens': 375, 'total_tokens': 6932}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected (ValueError): Interactive command kubectl edit detected. Such commands are not supported.', id='8c873644-358f-4059-98d2-be1d8c0257ad', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-85a5ff3950790418'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='02e92114-6015-49a6-94d7-71f1f7f35177'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to fix the MongoDB pod that\'s crashing. From the previous steps, they checked the pod\'s logs and found that the container is failing because it can\'t find the TLS certificate. The ConfigMap \'url-shorten-mongodb\' has a reference to /etc/tls/tls.pem, but the Secret \'mongodb-tls\' exists with the actual TLS files. However, the pod\'s volume mounts don\'t include the Secret, only the ConfigMap.\n\nSo the problem is that the Secret isn\'t mounted into the pod. The MongoDB container needs access to the TLS files, which are stored in the Secret. The solution should be to add a volume mount for the \'mongodb-tls\' Secret in the Deployment\'s pod spec. \n\nSince the user can\'t use \'kubectl edit\' directly, they need to update the Deployment YAML. The next step is to get the current Deployment configuration to modify it. Using \'kubectl get deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network -o yaml\' will retrieve the current spec. Then, they can add the Secret as a volume and mount it to the correct path. After making the changes, apply the updated YAML to the cluster. \n\nWait, but the user can\'t edit the Deployment directly. So they need to modify the YAML, add the Secret volume, and then apply it. The correct tool here is \'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\' to get the Deployment\'s current configuration, then apply the changes. But since the user can\'t edit interactively, they have to generate the correct command to update the Deployment with the new volume mount.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\ntool call: {"command": "kubectl get deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network -o yaml"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 370, 'prompt_tokens': 5647, 'total_tokens': 6017, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-a3b5-71a2-a57f-764498d35169-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5647, 'output_tokens': 370, 'total_tokens': 6017}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='ace54245-41a0-47d4-bc16-504f788f3048'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to fix a MongoDB pod that's crashing with a CrashLoopBackOff status. From the previous steps, they checked the pod's logs and description, found that the container is crashing because it can't find the TLS certificate. They looked into the ConfigMap and found that the MongoDB configuration points to /etc/tls/tls.pem. Then they checked the Secrets in the namespace and found a mongodb-tls secret that has tls.pem, but when they described the secret, it shows that the data is there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn't mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is using the tls.pem from the secret, but the pod's volumes aren't set up to mount the secret. So even though the secret exists, the container doesn't have access to it because it's not mounted. The user needs to check the pod's volume mounts to see if the secret is attached. \n\nBut the user already used kubectl describe pod and saw that the volume mounts include the ConfigMap but not the Secret. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn't. So the solution would be to update the pod's spec to include the secret as a volume mount. However, the user can't modify the pod directly; they need to update the Deployment or StatefulSet that's managing it. \n\nSince the user is supposed to submit the root cause, they should explain that the mongodb-tls secret exists but isn't mounted to /etc/tls/, causing MongoDB to fail. The user should be informed to mount the secret in the pod's configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-82b8812089902d7d', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 379, 'prompt_tokens': 6706, 'total_tokens': 7085, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-b552-7ff3-886e-2e1486993f9e-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployment url-shorten-mongodb -n social-network -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-82b8812089902d7d', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6706, 'output_tokens': 379, 'total_tokens': 7085}), ToolMessage(content='apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  annotations:\n    deployment.kubernetes.io/revision: "1"\n    meta.helm.sh/release-name: social-network\n    meta.helm.sh/release-namespace: social-network\n  creationTimestamp: "2026-03-17T12:18:27Z"\n  generation: 3\n  labels:\n    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm\n    service: url-shorten-mongodb\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\n  namespace: social-network\n  resourceVersion: "166109"\n  uid: f3dc51d3-9da7-43d5-87f2-8a22ea282f03\nspec:\n  progressDeadlineSeconds: 600\n  replicas: 1\n  revisionHistoryLimit: 10\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      service: url-shorten-mongodb\n  strategy:\n    rollingUpdate:\n      maxSurge: 25%\n      maxUnavailable: 25%\n    type: RollingUpdate\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      creationTimestamp: null\n      labels:\n        app: url-shorten-mongodb\n        service: url-shorten-mongodb\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - args:\n        - --config\n        - /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\n        image: docker.io/library/mongo:4.4.6\n        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 27017\n          protocol: TCP\n        resources: {}\n        terminationMessagePath: /dev/termination-log\n        terminationMessagePolicy: File\n        volumeMounts:\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\n          subPath: mongod.conf\n      dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst\n      hostname: url-shorten-mongodb\n      restartPolicy: Always\n      schedulerName: default-scheduler\n      securityContext: {}\n      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30\n      volumes:\n      - configMap:\n          defaultMode: 420\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\nstatus:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T12:18:28Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T12:19:18Z"\n    message: ReplicaSet "url-shorten-mongodb-ccd7bb58d" has successfully progressed.\n    reason: NewReplicaSetAvailable\n    status: "True"\n    type: Progressing\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T12:20:43Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T12:20:43Z"\n    message: Deployment does not have minimum availability.\n    reason: MinimumReplicasUnavailable\n    status: "False"\n    type: Available\n  observedGeneration: 3\n  replicas: 1\n  unavailableReplicas: 1\n  updatedReplicas: 1\n', id='c6c5d85d-d513-4c4d-a593-51d3d2302366', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-82b8812089902d7d'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='f90ade28-3e69-402a-a74c-2f1f99aaae2f'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The MongoDB pod is crashing because of a TLS certificate issue. The configmap points to /etc/tls/tls.pem, but the secret mongodb-tls exists. However, the pod\'s volume mounts only include the configmap, not the secret. So the secret isn\'t mounted, leading to the missing file error.\n\nThe deployment\'s template has a volumeMounts section that mounts the configmap to /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf. But the secret needs to be mounted to /etc/tls/ to provide the tls.pem file. The current setup doesn\'t include the secret in the volume mounts. \n\nTo fix this, I need to update the deployment\'s pod spec to add a volume mount for the mongodb-tls secret. Then, apply the changes. Since I can\'t use interactive commands, I\'ll generate the correct kubectl command to edit the deployment and add the secret mount. After that, wait a bit for the changes to take effect and check if the pod is fixed.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\ntool call: {"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      volumes:\\n      - configMap:\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n      - secret:\\n          name: mongodb-tls\\n        name: mongodb-tls-secret\\n      containers:\\n      - name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        volumeMounts:\\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n          subPath: mongod.conf\\n        - mountPath: /etc/tls\\n          name: mongodb-tls-secret\\nEOF"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 404, 'prompt_tokens': 6494, 'total_tokens': 6898, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-ca19-72d1-9658-ed1a7f06f09c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6494, 'output_tokens': 404, 'total_tokens': 6898}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4f2d79e7-41be-441b-be62-b9b76d009b48'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to fix a MongoDB pod that's crashing due to a missing TLS certificate. From the previous steps, they checked the pod's logs and found that the container can't find the TLS certificate. They looked into the ConfigMap and saw that the MongoDB config points to /etc/tls/tls.pem. Then they checked the Secrets and found a mongodb-tls secret with tls.pem, but when they described the secret, it showed the data was there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn't mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn't. So the MongoDB container doesn't have access to the TLS files because the secret isn't attached. The user needs to update the pod's volume mounts to include the secret. \n\nIn the Deployment YAML, the volumes section only has the ConfigMap. They need to add a new volume for the secret and mount it to /etc/tls. The container's volumeMounts should include a mount for the secret. So the fix is to modify the Deployment to add the secret volume and mount it correctly. \n\nThe user tried to apply a modified Deployment with the secret volume, but the tool response might not have confirmed success. They need to check if the Deployment was updated. Maybe they should verify the changes by describing the pod or deployment again. Alternatively, they could wait for the pod to restart and check if the issue is resolved. If the pod still crashes, they might need to check the logs again or ensure the secret is correctly referenced in the mount path.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      volumes:\\n      - configMap:\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n      - secret:\\n          name: mongodb-tls\\n        name: mongodb-tls-secret\\n      containers:\\n      - name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        volumeMounts:\\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n          subPath: mongod.conf\\n        - mountPath: /etc/tls\\n          name: mongodb-tls-secret\\nEOF"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-986a2bb116fb7e5f', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 527, 'prompt_tokens': 7709, 'total_tokens': 8236, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-ddc0-7e02-a3ae-fff3ee3e70d1-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\n  namespace: social-network\nspec:\n  template:\n    spec:\n      volumes:\n      - configMap:\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\n      - secret:\n          name: mongodb-tls\n        name: mongodb-tls-secret\n      containers:\n      - name: url-shorten-mongodb\n        volumeMounts:\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\n          subPath: mongod.conf\n        - mountPath: /etc/tls\n          name: mongodb-tls-secret\nEOF'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-986a2bb116fb7e5f', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7709, 'output_tokens': 527, 'total_tokens': 8236}), ToolMessage(content="Dry-run failed. Potentially it's an invalid command. stderr: Warning: resource deployments/url-shorten-mongodb is missing the kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration annotation which is required by kubectl apply. kubectl apply should only be used on re... [truncated]", id='cf00ba94-be3b-407f-9486-7fa6d1e7d3b3', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-986a2bb116fb7e5f'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='eab67c7e-f2b3-4660-ba79-61b661c9f76e')]]
