 mounted to /etc/tls/ to provide the tls.pem file. The current setup doesn\'t include the secret in the volume mounts. \n\nTo fix this, I need to update the deployment\'s pod spec to add a volume mount for the mongodb-tls secret. Then, apply the changes. Since I can\'t use interactive commands, I\'ll generate the correct kubectl command to edit the deployment and add the secret mount. After that, wait a bit for the changes to take effect and check if the pod is fixed.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\ntool call: {"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      volumes:\\n      - configMap:\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n      - secret:\\n          name: mongodb-tls\\n        name: mongodb-tls-secret\\n      containers:\\n      - name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        volumeMounts:\\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/mongod.conf\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n          subPath: mongod.conf\\n        - mountPath: /etc/tls\\n          name: mongodb-tls-secret\\nEOF"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 404, 'prompt_tokens': 6494, 'total_tokens': 6898, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbc0-ca19-72d1-9658-ed1a7f06f09c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6494, 'output_tokens': 404, 'total_tokens': 6898}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4f2d79e7-41be-441b-be62-b9b76d009b48'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to fix a MongoDB pod that's crashing due to a missing TLS certificate. From the previous steps, they checked the pod's logs and found that the container can't find the TLS certificate. They looked into the ConfigMap and saw that the MongoDB config points to /etc/tls/tls.pem. Then they checked the Secrets and found a mongodb-tls secret with tls.pem, but when they described the secret, it showed the data was there.\n\nWait, but the problem is that the secret isn't mounted into the pod. The ConfigMap is mounted, but the Secret isn't. So the MongoDB container doesn't have access to the TLS files because the secret isn't attached. The user needs to update the pod's volume mounts to include the secret. \n\nIn the Deployment YAML, the volumes section only has the ConfigMap. They need to add a new volume for the secret and mount it to /etc/tls. The container's volumeMounts should include a mount for the secret. So the fix is to modify the Deployment to add the secret volume and mount it correctly. \n\nThe user tried to apply a modified Deployment with the secret volume, but the tool response might not have confirmed success. They need to check if the Deployment was updated. Maybe they should verify the changes by describing the pod or deployment again. Alternatively, they could wait for the pod to restart and check if the issue is resolved. If the pod still crashes, they might need to check the logs again or ensure the secret is correctly referenced in the mount path.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      volumes:\\n      - configMap:\\n          name: url-shorten-mongodb\\n        name: url-shorten-mongodb-config\\n      - secret:\\n          name: mongodb-tls\\n        name: mongodb-tls-secret